S10.2D-R8.3 target aggregate reader ownership diagnosis

The first mark-ready attempt stopped before its readiness state update with
TARGET_AGGREGATE_STATE_RED. The runtime-control state remained PENDING, real
acquisition remained false, and its baseline remained null.

The aggregate file was a regular, single-link, mode-0600 chatops-owned file.
The new target reader invoked the Application counter as root, while the
counter deliberately rejects aggregate material whose owner differs from its
effective user. The existing source-reader contract already used chatops.

The bounded correction runs the target reader as chatops with the same pinned
Application source and path. It does not alter aggregate contents, services,
database rows, evidence, Application source, or product boundaries.
